      "content": "hey, im looking at some candidate bios for a senior management role at a tech firm. i need to get a feel for how these sound to an executive audience. can u look at these two summaries and tell me which one comes off as more professional and authoritative for a leadership position? basically, i need to know if the tone fits a high-level exec.\n\nBio 1:\n\"I have consistently demonstrated a capacity for strategic oversight and cross-functional team leadership. My expertise lies in streamlining operational workflows to maximize efficiency while maintaining strict adherence to budgetary constraints and long-term corporate objectives.\"\n\nBio 2:\n\"I been leadin' teams and makin sure all the projects stay on track for years now. I know how to get things done right without messin' up the budget, and I always make sure the team is movin' in the right direction to hit our goals.\"",
